usage: act_ci.py [-h] [--pr PR] [--repo REPO] [--worktree WORKTREE]
                 [--workflow {all,docs,elaborate,rtl-fast,rtl-full}]
                 [--cpu-ranges CPU_RANGES] [--jobs JOBS] [--job-cpus JOB_CPUS]
                 [--job-memory JOB_MEMORY] [--act-bin ACT_BIN]
                 [--evidence-directory EVIDENCE_DIRECTORY]
                 [--trusted-install-sha256 TRUSTED_INSTALL_SHA256] [--sudo]
                 [--slot SLOT] [--slot-root SLOT_ROOT] [--dry-run]
                 [--selftest] [--interrupt-selftest] [--boundary-selftest]

Run this repository's GitHub workflows locally at one exact PR head. The
runner is host-side security code. Invoke the copy from a clean trusted
``dev`` worktree, never the copy in the pull request being tested. It refuses
unless that trusted worktree is the validation base: the live remote ``dev``
tip resolved once at invocation. GitHub's recorded PR base oid is frozen when
the PR is opened, so it never refuses a run: it is printed, it selects which
note is printed, and it is the base SHA in the generated event, because that
payload feeds scope classification and hosted receives the recorded value.
Candidate files are fetched without credentials into a fresh per-run
repository and are only executed by ``act`` inside unprivileged containers
with no Docker socket, ambient configuration, host secrets, or persistent
writable cache. Typical use, from the candidate worktree:: python3 -I
/path/to/trusted-dev/scripts/act_ci.py --pr 268 python3 -I /path/to/trusted-
dev/scripts/act_ci.py --pr 268 --workflow rtl-full python3 -I
/path/to/trusted-dev/scripts/act_ci.py --pr 268 --dry-run Use ``--sudo`` only
on hosts whose Docker socket is unavailable to the current user. ``--slot N``
(1-63, with ``--sudo``) replays against a Docker daemon this invocation starts
and stops in its own network namespace, so replays in different slots run side
by side; slot 0, the default, is the default local daemon exactly as before.
The environment never selects a daemon: an invoking environment carrying
DOCKER_HOST, DOCKER_CONTEXT or DOCKER_CONFIG is refused:: python3 -I
/path/to/trusted-dev/scripts/act_ci.py --pr 268 --sudo --slot 1 Exit 0 means
every selected workflow passed; exit 1 means a workflow failed; exit 2 is a
setup, trust-boundary, cleanup, or exact-head refusal. A handled terminal
signal returns ``128 + signum`` only after cleanup; SIGINT therefore returns
130 and names itself in the final diagnostic.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --pr PR               open pull-request number
  --repo REPO           OWNER/REPO (default: trusted gh repository)
  --worktree WORKTREE   candidate worktree to cross-check (default: current
                        directory)
  --workflow {all,docs,elaborate,rtl-fast,rtl-full}
                        workflow alias; repeatable (default: all)
  --cpu-ranges CPU_RANGES
                        manager-booked aligned CPU ranges, comma-separated
  --jobs JOBS           job containers run at once, 1-8 (default 4)
  --job-cpus JOB_CPUS   each job's booked CPU range width: 16 (ranges of 16 or
                        12), 8 (ranges of 8), 6 (ranges of 6) (default 16)
  --job-memory JOB_MEMORY
                        each job container's memory and swap cap in GiB, 1-8
                        (default 8); jobs times it plus 4 must fit 36
  --act-bin ACT_BIN     trusted act executable
  --evidence-directory EVIDENCE_DIRECTORY
                        new durable directory outside the candidate tree
                        (default: private temporary directory)
  --trusted-install-sha256 TRUSTED_INSTALL_SHA256
                        SHA-256 of an independently audited immutable runner
                        install; bootstrap only, never point this at the
                        candidate worktree
  --sudo                run Docker and act through non-interactive sudo
  --slot SLOT           replay slot 0-63: 0 (the default) is the default local
                        Docker daemon; any other starts this invocation's own
                        daemon in its own network namespace (requires --sudo)
  --slot-root SLOT_ROOT
                        root-owned directory, with root-owned ancestors and no
                        symlink, holding each isolated slot's persistent data-
                        root (default /var/lib/milan-act-ci)
  --dry-run             materialize and print exact act commands without
                        running them
  --selftest            run offline negative and construction tests
  --interrupt-selftest  SIGINT a frozen live act job and verify cleanup
                        (requires Docker)
  --boundary-selftest   plant operator secrets, prove the boundaried probe job
                        and git see none, then prove the same probe sees them
                        once the boundary is removed (requires Docker)
